---
# Pin the collector to the node's real NVMe. A privileged pod sees the HOST's /dev, which
# on a Longhorn node includes dozens of iSCSI virtual disks (sda, sdb, …) — smartctl
# errors on every one (checksum error, exit 4) and publishes bogus 0x600… wwn records.
# `allow_listed_devices` is the key that restricts the smartctl scan (a `devices:` list
# only CUSTOMIZES detected entries — tried first, and the scan kept publishing the iSCSI
# fleet). Both nodes' NVMe enumerates as /dev/nvme0, so one config serves the whole
# DaemonSet. The Docker-era collector read the same device from a per-host inventory
# variable; this ConfigMap is the only place it is set now.
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: scrutiny-collector-config
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
data:
  collector.yaml: |
    version: 1
    allow_listed_devices:
      - /dev/nvme0
